Z||000001||artherd||06-28-2001||05:15 AM||||Hiya Corinne, I've got Carbonmet Carbon/metal pads from the fierostore, and they work very well, best part is the brake dust. It's not nearly as nasty as normal brake pad dust!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000002||Will||06-28-2001||08:17 AM||||I've got Performance Friction carbomets on GA brakes all around, and they work well; pretty easy to modulate the brakes.<P>Don't semi-metallics have to be pretty darn hot before they start to work well?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wannabe||06-28-2001||09:00 AM||||KVR offers and excellent carbo-met pad with kevlar backing. Perfect for the street and even work well with limited use on the track (KVR does not recommend these for the track though) Very reasonably priced. <A HREF="http://www.kvrperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kvrperformance.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||06-28-2001||09:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B>Don't semi-metallics have to be pretty darn hot before they start to work well?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No.  Metallic brakes have to be hot to work well.  Semi-metallics are a hybrid specially made to give the high heat performance and still work well when cold.  I've run semi-metallics on my old Firebirds and Trans Ams for years without problems.||||reg||6
Z||000005||stsmithgt||06-28-2001||09:53 AM||||I have semi-metallic brakes, and I find they work better when there not cold that's for sure.  I like them a whole lot better than standard break pads because I can't stand brake fade.  I think that's why I have a car that doesn't know what a drum brake is. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I usually give my brakes touch when I think I might be using them pretty hard, like on my favorite off ramp <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, especially if it's wet out to make sure they're dry when I need them.  It does make a difference when your pushing the cars limitations.(ok mine too.)<P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
